From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Will Faust <willtechnoduck@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 12:27:44 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] FEX: publish the runtime diagnostic switch through the Mono
 bridge

Adds diag_enabled to the shared contract and bumps IOS_MONO_ABI_VERSION to 2,
since the struct grew.

The ABI guard earned its place immediately. Adding this field and rebuilding
only the unix side left the shipped FEX compiled against version 1, so
BTCpu64IosSetMonoBridge refused the pointer, the bridge never armed, and the
SWPAL storm returned in full - 5,411,000 emulated stores against 806,912. That
is a clean, reversible perf regression instead of FEX reading a struct whose
every field past abi_version had shifted four bytes, inside a Mach fault
handler.

The rule that follows: touching ios_mono_bridge.h means rebuilding FEX, always.
Bumping the ABI turns silent corruption into a loud failure; it does not spare
you the rebuild.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Madeira-commit: 4cc5afe2bf35edc1f7adf256bb48ed6e3d800c3e
Rebased: clean
Class: madeira-port
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-09-24-fex-latest-rebase.md
Offered-upstream: no
---
 Source/Windows/ARM64EC/IosMonoBridge.h | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Source/Windows/ARM64EC/IosMonoBridge.h b/Source/Windows/ARM64EC/IosMonoBridge.h
index 3f7e4f7..b5e3e77 100644
--- a/Source/Windows/ARM64EC/IosMonoBridge.h
+++ b/Source/Windows/ARM64EC/IosMonoBridge.h
@@ -16,7 +16,7 @@
 #pragma once
 #include <cstdint>
 
-#define IOS_MONO_ABI_VERSION 1
+#define IOS_MONO_ABI_VERSION 2
 #define IOS_MONO_MAX_ALIASES 4096
 #define IOS_MONO_MAX_CONTEXTS 64
 
@@ -39,6 +39,7 @@ struct ios_mono_pending {
 
 struct ios_mono_bridge {
   uint32_t abi_version;
+  uint32_t diag_enabled;  // ml649: runtime diagnostic switch
   uint32_t off_inline_jit_block_header;
   uint32_t off_block_tail;
   uint32_t off_tail_rip;
